su'o da

First, you want "lo se du'u", not "lo du'u".  retsku, like its brother
cusku, wants a text, not a fact for what it states.  Also , why use "sei fi
la jbofi'e"  retsku already has the questionee as part of it.  So the sei is
really unnecessary (although not incorrect, per se).  Another stylistic
point:  I'd probably have had alyn say "na'i" instead of .ie nai, but that's
just me.
                    --gejyspa
